{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_5acff58c8613ca0def4dfa59a354928b4baf607df92d513f8468842774cd996c", "title": "Edwin Brown (actor)", "text": "He had a lengthy career in television, often playing policemen or similar roles. His film roles included a prison warder in the comedy \"Two-Way Stretch\" (1960), and Albert Pierrepoint, the hangman, in \"10 Rillington Place\" (1971).", "score": 19.2938}, {"id": "hp_doc_3d4f78f9f5fc4289325da4aefa77cdb4a9ff033927f5b076a9565a95e6d3462b", "title": "Albert Pierrepoint", "text": "Albert Pierrepoint ( ; 30 March 1905 – 10 July 1992) was a long-serving hangman in England. He executed at least 400 people, including William Joyce (\"Lord Haw-Haw\") and John Amery. In Germany and Austria, after the Second World War, he executed some 200 people who had been convicted of war crimes. In England, Pierrepoint hanged Timothy Evans for a crime committed by his neighbour John Christie, who was also hanged by Pierrepoint.", "score": 14.511}, {"id": "hp_doc_0f88309dce7abdba24b8a66139e23305e521be99f8b68c242c3f5d9e3f7321bb", "title": "Tangled: The Series", "text": "Tangled: The Series is an American animated musical fantasy television series that premiered on Disney Channel on March 10, 2017 as a movie, and began airing regular episodes from March 24, 2017. It is based on Disney's 2010 computer-animated film \"Tangled\" directed by Nathan Greno and Byron Howard. It takes place between the original movie and the short \"Tangled Ever After\". A teaser trailer was released during the Disney Channel Original Movie, \"The Swap\". It began as a Disney Channel Original Movie, titled \"\", which premiered on March 10, 2017.", "score": 7.7791}], "remaining_searches": 1}
